🔢 General Math

    1 KB = 10³ bytes (~1000)
    1 MB = 10⁶ bytes (~10⁶)
    1 GB = 10⁹ bytes (~10⁹)
    1 TB = 10¹² bytes (~10¹²)
    1 PB = 10¹⁵ bytes
    1 million (M) = 10⁶
    1 billion (B) = 10⁹

⚡ Latency Reference (approx)

    L1 cache access → ~0.5 ns
    L2 cache access → ~7 ns
    RAM access → ~100 ns
    SSD read → ~100 μs (0.1 ms)
    Disk read → ~10 ms
    Network (LAN) → ~0.1 ms
    Network (Cross DC) → ~100 ms

    👉 Rule: RAM ≈ 100x faster than disk, disk ≈ 100x faster than network

📦 Storage & Content Sizes

    1 page of text ≈ 2 KB
    1 email ≈ 100 KB
    1 image (compressed) ≈ 500 KB
    1 song (MP3) ≈ 5 MB
    1 HD movie (2 hrs, compressed) ≈ 3 GB
    1 4K movie ≈ 20 GB
    1 profile (user + metadata) ≈ 1 KB – 10 KB

    👉 Rule of thumb: 1 TB disk ≈ 200k HD movies OR 300M images

📈 Throughput & QPS

    QPS (Queries per second) = RPS × Users
    1M DAU → ~10 QPS (low activity app)
    10M DAU → ~100 QPS (social app)
    100M DAU → ~1K–10K QPS (FB/Twitter scale)

    👉 Estimation: Peak QPS ≈ 5× Average QPS

💾 Database Storage

Row in DB → 100 bytes – 1 KB
1M rows ≈ 1 GB (if row = 1 KB)
1B rows ≈ 1 TB

Write throughput:

    MySQL single node → ~10k writes/sec
    Cassandra / DynamoDB → 100k+ writes/sec